{"type":"text","timestamp":1792482774972,"sessionID":"ses_ea7b49377ffeDBKJYjlIv62mLB","part":{"id":"prt_1584c7e7a001T42aVdrKN4ZJy1","messageID":"msg_1584c7437001v6Xc6FotHA377w","sessionID":"ses_ea7b49377ffeDBKJYjlIv62mLB","type":"text","text":"The complete Zephyr RTOS DMA application has been written to `submission/main.c`.\n\nThe application implements all requirements:\n\n1. **Obtains DMA controller** from devicetree using `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(dma0))`\n2. **Checks device readiness** with `device_is_ready()` before use\n3. **Initializes buffers** - 64-byte source with pattern (0xA5, 0xA4, ...), destination with zeros\n4. **Configures DMA** for memory-to-memory transfer using `dma_config()` and `dma_start()`\n5. **Uses callback** (`dma_callback`) to signal completion via semaphore\n6. **Waits with timeout** (1000ms) using `k_sem_take()`\n7. **Verifies transfer** by comparing destination against source byte-by-byte\n8. **Prints results** - \"DMA transfer SUCCEEDED\" or \"DMA transfer FAILED\"\n9. **Handles errors** at each step with descriptive messages and appropriate error codes\n\nThe code is production-ready with proper alignment for DMA buffers, comprehensive error handling, and clear status reporting.","time":{"start":1792482770554,"end":1792482774963}}}
